      "side": 0,
      "message": "Thanks a tonne for the detailed explanation, that makes a lot more sense to me now. However, I do worry about explicit users of the `freezer_do_not_count()` API -- for example, binder seems to use that around a normal call to `schedule()` and who knows what folks could be doing in their own modules.\n\nSo I fear that this approach is likely to be incomplete.\n\nAn alternative would be to skip the reschedule for these tasks, but I\u0027m having trouble narrowing things down enough that this wouldn\u0027t cause a preemption issue where we continuously run the same task because it always has a signal pending. Hrmph.",
